+
+## Android Provider Forms
+
+`test-provider-forms-android.sh` starts an isolated daemon in a fresh temporary
+`PASEO_HOME`, adds an `adb reverse` mapping for its random port, and runs
+`provider-forms-android.yaml` against an installed Paseo Android development
+build. The flow opens Settings > Providers and verifies the list plus the
+OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic-compatible, and ACP custom-provider forms without
+saving a provider. After Maestro exits, the harness queries the daemon snapshot
+and asserts that cancellation left only the required Codex entry; the raw JSON
+and command stderr remain in the artifact directory.
+
+```bash
+bash packages/app/maestro/test-provider-forms-android.sh
+```
+
+Run the device-independent flow/harness contract check with:
+
+```bash
+bash packages/app/maestro/test-provider-forms-android.sh --check
+```
+
+The harness does not invoke `scripts/dev-daemon.sh` and never reads or writes
+the worktree's `.dev/paseo-home` or `.paseo-dev`. Start the development build's
+Metro server before running it. Set `PASEO_MAESTRO_SERIAL` when multiple Android
+devices are attached.
